
# Library Directory - ESP32-S3-POE-ETH-8DI-8DO Project

This directory contains all external libraries required for the ESP32-S3-POE-ETH-8DI-8DO project.

## 📦 Libraries Included

- **Adafruit_NeoPixel** - RGB LED (WS2812B) control via 1-wire protocol
- **ArduinoJson** - JSON parsing and serialization
- **pubsubclient** - MQTT broker client library
- **WiFiManager** - WiFi configuration and connection management
- **ModbusMaster** - Modbus RTU protocol for RS485 communication
- **Universal-Arduino-Telegram-Bot** - Telegram bot integration
- **HTTPClient** - HTTP/HTTPS client for web requests
- **WiFiClientSecure** - Secure WiFi connections (SSL/TLS)
- **ESP32-S3-POE-ETH-8DI-8DO** - Custom library for board control (main project library)

## 🚀 Quick Start

### Option 1: Automatic Installation (Recommended)

Run the provided shell script to clone all required libraries:

```bash
cd lib/
./clone_repo.sh
```

**What the script does:**
- ✓ Checks git and curl availability
- ✓ Clones all required libraries from GitHub
- ✓ Updates existing libraries if already present
- ✓ Verifies successful installation
- ✓ Provides colored console output for easy reading

**Requirements:**
- `git` installed on your system
- `curl` installed on your system
- Internet connection

### Option 2: Manual Installation

Clone individual libraries as needed:

```bash
# Install Adafruit NeoPixel
git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit_NeoPixel.git

# Install ArduinoJson
git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/bblanchon/ArduinoJson.git

# Install MQTT Client
git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/knolleary/pubsubclient.git

# Install WiFi Manager
git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/tzapu/WiFiManager.git

# Install Modbus Master
git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/4-20ma/ModbusMaster.git
```

## 📂 Directory Structure

```
lib/
├── README                           ← This file
├── clone_repo.sh                    ← Automatic installation script
├── Adafruit_NeoPixel/               ← RGB LED control
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── Adafruit_NeoPixel.h
│   │   └── Adafruit_NeoPixel.cpp
│   └── examples/
├── ArduinoJson/                     ← JSON library
├── pubsubclient/                    ← MQTT library
├── WiFiManager/                     ← WiFi configuration
├── ModbusMaster/                    ← RS485 Modbus protocol
├── Universal-Arduino-Telegram-Bot/  ← Telegram integration
├── HTTPClient/                      ← HTTP client
├── WiFiClientSecure/                ← Secure WiFi
└── ESP32-S3-POE-ETH-8DI-8DO/        ← Main custom library
    ├── src/
    │   ├── ESP32S3_8DI8DO.h
    │   └── ESP32S3_8DI8DO.cpp
    └── examples/
```

## 🛠 PlatformIO Configuration

The `platformio.ini` file is configured to:
- Use `lib_extra_dirs = ${PROJECT_DIR}/lib` to search in this directory
- Automatically include necessary dependencies
- Ignore conflicting libraries with `lib_ignore`

## 💡 Usage Example

```cpp
#include <Arduino.h>
#include "ESP32-S3-POE-ETH-8DI-8DO.h"

ESP32S3_8DI8DO board;

void setup() {
    Serial.begin(115200);
    board.begin();
    
    // Control RGB LED
    board.getRGB().setColor(255, 0, 0);  // Red
    
    // Beep buzzer
    board.buzzer_beep(3);  // 3 beeps
}

void loop() {
    board.loop();
    
    // Read digital input
    bool di_state = board.getDI().read(0);
    
    // Set digital output
    board.getDO().write(0, HIGH);
}
```

## 🔧 Troubleshooting

### Script won't run
```bash
chmod +x clone_repo.sh
```

### Permission denied
Make sure you have write permissions in the lib/ directory:
```bash
chmod 755 /path/to/lib
```

### Libraries not found during compile
1. Ensure all libraries are cloned successfully
2. Run `platformio run --target clean` to rebuild cache
3. Verify library paths in VS Code IntelliSense settings

### Specific library issues
- **Adafruit_NeoPixel**: Requires ESP32 core > 2.0.0
- **ModbusMaster**: Requires RS485 hardware connected
- **WiFiManager**: May conflict with some WiFi libraries

